<% page_title "Privacy" %>

<article class="wrap measure">
  <h1 class="text-4xl">Privacy</h1>

  <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-ink-600">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">What we store</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2">
        <li>Your name and email, to run your account.</li>
        <li>Your subscription, orders and download history, because that is the licence record.</li>
        <li>IP addresses in hashed form only, attached to audit events and downloads.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">What we do not do</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2">
        <li>No third-party analytics, advertising pixels, or session recording. None ship in this application.</li>
        <li>No selling or sharing of personal data.</li>
        <li>No personal data in URLs, in search indexes, or in error reports.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink-950">Your controls</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        In your account you can see every consent you have given, and request an export or
        deletion of your data. A deletion request removes your personal details; the download
        and order records that back the licence remain, because they are the evidence that a
        licence was granted.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        <%= link_to "Manage your data", account_root_path, class: "underline" %> (sign-in required).
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>
